{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 External Window Docker\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Embed external application windows (browsers, media players, etc.) directly into REAPER's docker system.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Features\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Launch URLs in app mode (Edge/Chrome) and auto-embed\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Embed any detected window (Spotify, YouTube, Discord, etc.)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Favorites and URL history with right-click management\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Customizable theme colors and header height\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Keyboard shortcut support (via companion script)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Re-embed last URL on startup\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Find Window by Title for hard-to-detect windows\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGui\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab js_ReaScriptAPI\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Usage\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Run this script from the Actions list\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Dock the "External Window Docker" window\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Click "Open Menu" to access all features\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Use "Open & Embed" to launch and dock browser content\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Keyboard Shortcut\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Install the companion script "CK_ExternalWindowDocker_ToggleMenu" and assign it a keyboard shortcut via Actions > Show action list.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Markers to Take Markers\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Copies project markers that fall within selected media items' time ranges and applies them as take markers on each item's active take, preserving marker names and colors.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Usage\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Place project markers on the timeline with descriptive names\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Select one or more media items\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Run this script\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab A dialog will ask whether to remove the original project markers\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Notes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Only markers within each item's time range are copied\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Accounts for take start offset and playrate per item\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Works with multiple selected items at once\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Requires REAPER v5.20+ (SetTakeMarker API)\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaPack Repository Template\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A template for GitHub-hosted ReaPack repositories with automated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack-index
}}}
 running from GitHub Actions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Replace the name of the repository in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "/index.xml"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
index.xml
}}}
 when using this template. This will be the name shown in ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 <index version="1" name="Name of your repository here">\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Replace the contents of this file ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "/README.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
README.md
}}}
). This will be the text shown when using ReaPack's "About this repository" feature.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 reapack-index looks for package files in subfolders. The folder tree represents the package categories shown in ReaPack.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each package file is expected to begin with a metadata header. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index/wiki/Packaging-Documentation"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Packaging Documentation
}}}
 on reapack-index's wiki.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The URL to import in ReaPack is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-repository-template/raw/master/index.xml"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
https://github.com/{\f1 <your username>}/{\f1 <repository name>}/raw/master/index.xml
}}}
.\par}
}
